---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Advanced: Time Complexity & Naming | Bubble Sort">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-6 sm:py-10 space-y-8">
    {/* Page Header */}
    <div class="text-center space-y-3">
      <span class="bg-focusBg border border-focusBorder text-focusText text-xs font-extrabold px-3 py-1 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wider">
        Optional Bonus Module • For Curious Minds
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">
        Advanced: <span class="text-accent font-handwritten text-4xl sm:text-6xl">Time Complexity & Naming</span> 🤓
      </h1>
      <p class="text-textSecondary text-sm sm:text-base max-w-xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        Yeh section optional hai! Agar tum exam ya interview context samajhna chahte ho, toh yahan toggles khol kar dekho.
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* Section 1: Naming & Etymology */}
    <div class="bg-card border border-textSecondary/20 rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-main flex items-center gap-2">
        <span>🧼</span> Kyun Bolte Hain "Bubble Sort"?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-main leading-relaxed">
        Jaise cold drink ya paani mein halke air bubbles upar ki taraf float karke surface par aate hain, 
        waise hi bubble sort mein har pass ke baad sabse bada number (heavy element) sliding pairs swap ho kar 
        end par (surface par) <strong>"bubble up"</strong> kar jata hai! Isi analogy se iska naam Bubble Sort pada.
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* Section 2: Time Complexity Collapsible Box */}
    <details class="bg-card border border-textSecondary/20 rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm group cursor-pointer">
      <summary class="font-bold text-lg text-main flex items-center justify-between list-none">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>⏱️</span> Time Complexity: O(N²) Kyun Hai? (Click to reveal)
        </span>
        <span class="text-accent group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
      </summary>

      <div class="pt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-textSecondary/15 mt-4">
        <div class="dhyan-do-box p-4 rounded-xl space-y-1">
          <p class="font-bold">Worst & Average Case: O(N²)</p>
          <p className="text-xs">
            Agar list completely reversed order mein hai (e.g. 5, 4, 3, 2, 1), toh har pass mein (N-1) comparisons 
            karne padte hain. Total comparisons ~ N × (N-1) / 2 = <strong>O(N²)</strong>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-focusBg border border-focusBorder text-focusText p-4 rounded-xl space-y-1">
          <p class="font-bold">Best Case: O(N)</p>
          <p className="text-xs">
            Agar list pehle se 100% sorted hai (e.g. 1, 2, 3, 4, 5), toh pehle hi pass mein 0 swaps hongi aur algorithm 
            wahi ruk jayegi. Total comparisons = N-1 = <strong>O(N)</strong>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bg border border-textSecondary/30 p-4 rounded-xl space-y-1">
          <p class="font-bold text-main">Space Complexity: O(1)</p>
          <p className="text-xs text-textSecondary">
            Bubble sort ko koi alag se extra memory/array nahi chahiye hota. Bas usi array mein swapping hoti hai (In-place sorting).
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>

    {/* Navigation */}
    <div class="pt-4 text-center flex justify-center gap-4">
      <a
        href="/quiz"
        class="px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl border border-textSecondary/30 bg-bg text-main hover:border-accent text-sm font-semibold"
      >
        ← Back to Quiz
      </a>
      <a
        href="/complete"
        class="btn-primary px-7 py-2.5 rounded-xl text-sm font-bold shadow-sm"
      >
        Get Certificate →
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
